# In a file without types `function shape(width, options = {})` gave the parameter the checked type `{}`: use was not asked, the wire said "anything", and at the join of the default and the parameter the
# walk guessed the one layout that it saw: the empty literal's: wrong at every call that hands an object: five reads at their sites (230 instructions a call; 137 for the same function without the default).
# Use is asked as it is for any: the parameter is expected to be the literal that has the names (f1 = shape). What arrives is asked first and read by slots; the function's own literal is asked on the
# failing side; what is neither reads at its site.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = NewObject
# CHECK: = ShapeTest {{*}}[rejectsMarkedObjects]
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}}key="label" {{*}}level=Proven
# CHECK: = ShapeTest {{*}}[rejectsMarkedObjects]
# CHECK: = PropGet {{*}}key="label"
# CHECK: = GetSlot {{*}}key="depth"
